hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2832","Narrated to us Nasr ibn Marzuq, narrated to us Asad ibn Musa, narrated to us Isra'il.

And narrated to us Muhammad ibn Rafi', from Yahya ibn Adam, narrated to me Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn 'Abbas who said:

Ibn Rafi' said: Al-Fadl informed me that he was the riding companion (ridf) of the Prophet (ﷺ) when he departed from Muzdalifah. A Bedouin was accompanying him, and his riding companion was his beautiful daughter.

Al-Fadl said: So I began to look at her, whereupon the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) took my face and turned it away from her. He continued to recite the talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah al-'Aqabah.

Ibn Rafi' said: ""He was accompanying him"" or ""asking him.""

Abu Bakr said: Suwayn ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz al-Basri narrated it, and I am free from any responsibility regarding his narration or that of his father.

My father said: I heard him say: Narrated to me Ibn 'Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn 'Abbas, that he was the riding companion of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on the Day of 'Arafah. Al-Fadl began to glance at the women and look at them, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) began to turn his face away with his hand from behind him. The young man kept glancing at them, so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:

""O my nephew, indeed this is a day in which if someone restrains his hearing, sight, and tongue, he will be forgiven.""

---

**CHAPTER:**"
"2833","Narrated to us by Nasr ibn Marzuq, who narrated to us by Asad, who narrated to us by Sukayn ibn Abd al-Aziz."
"2834","###
 It was narrated to us by Ishaq bin Mansur, who informed us that Habban bin Hilal Abu Habib said: ""Sukayn al-Qattan narrated to us, from his father, who narrated from Ibn Abbas (RA), who said: 'Al-Fadl bin Abbas (RA) was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on the Day of Arafah. The young man (Al-Fadl) kept looking at the women, but the narrator (Sukayn) said: ""He turned"
